Anything that happens to me,

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:48.853
like my eye, for instance,

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:50.960
I let it heal on its own.

00:13:52.541 --> 00:13:53.374
You see my hand,

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.840
I broke my own hand

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:58.290
'cause I was mad at somebody,

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.300
and I punched a wall pretty hard in a gym.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.803
My whole knuckle,

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:07.960
my hand is not the same anymore,

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:09.610
if you could tell the difference.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:14.510
Because I chose to let it heal on its own.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:17.000
Now my hand is permanently damaged.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.360
I probably can't type 80
words a minute anymore,

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.010
but I can still type pretty good.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:24.470
I can't do certain things

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:25.940
that I used to

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.790
due to this

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.483
skin graft that I have.

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.030
The spider laid eggs in my arm

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.650
and the infection
because I waited too long

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.780
to go to the hospital,

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.210
my arm got so big.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.717
It was unbelievable.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:48.160
They skinned my arm.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:50.410
They took skin off of here,

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.753
whatever they cut off.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:56.320
And then they skin grafted from my leg.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.153
See.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:00.850
Everybody thought that

00:15:01.917 --> 00:15:02.860
I had been in a fire

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.910
because of the way my arm looks.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:06.550
But this is for everybody Downtown.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.310
This is a brown recluse spider

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:09.310
that did this to me.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.770
So, for those who are out
there and not showering

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:16.000
and not taking care of
themselves as much as possible,

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.150
this can happen to you.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:20.110
Whether it's on your face,

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:22.190
your ass, wherever,

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.690
you're gonna lose something.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:24.523
I know I did

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.253
because I chose drugs over my own health.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.060
I could have lost my right arm.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:38.170
Then I'd have to learn
how to live with one arm.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.890
And I'm not even left-handed

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:40.723
so that,

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:42.820
I don't know how hard it would be

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.870
to wipe my own ass with my left hand,

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:45.823
I've never done it.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.453
You know, I'm right-handed.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:16:00.090
Downtown has been the
downfall of my existence.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:06.460
I have lost, just Downtown alone,

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.970
I have lost so much.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:12.770
I lost all the trust from my family

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.270
just because of the addiction.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:16.150
Not because of what I've not

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:16.983
or what I've done

00:16:16.983 --> 00:16:18.340
or what I might have done,

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.450
but because they know

00:16:20.885 --> 00:16:22.770
what addiction can do to a person,

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:24.813
especially the addiction that I have.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:28.620
Anybody can make a change.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:29.570
You're never too old,

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.053
and not too young.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:33.230
If you can walk, talk,

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:34.400
and you're still breathing,

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.503
there's always a way.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:38.683
Always.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.970
But you have to want it

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:44.262
in order to get it.

00:16:44.262 --> 00:16:45.095
You can't just talk about it,

00:16:45.095 --> 00:16:46.920
you gotta put in work.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:47.963
And it's not easy.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:50.210
I know for me it's not.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.783
I've quit doing drugs for,

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.310
different periods of time.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:02.860
But then I always ended up
coming right back to it.

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:05.163
All it takes is one.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.840
And that one hit,

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.520
that one shot,

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.440
whatever it is that you do

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.393
can ruin your life forever.

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:18.430
I have no idea where any
of my family members are.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.263
I haven't seen my mother since 2011.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.260
I don't know where she is.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.060
My grandparents don't know where she is,

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.793
my uncles, nobody has a clue.

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:32.490
I don't know where any of my sisters are,

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:33.720
but my younger sister

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:37.590
that I grew up with from my mother,

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:39.763
she passed away in 2008.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.040
I was in prison,

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.490
I didn't even get a chance
to say goodbye to her.

00:17:49.185 --> 00:17:50.937
And the reason why I went to prison

00:17:50.937 --> 00:17:51.937
is for having drugs.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.970
My sister, she used to come down here

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.373
and beg me to come home.

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:12.110
And she would cry.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.270
And I'd lie to her

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:15.370
and tell her I'm gonna be there soon.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:16.913
And I would never show up.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.510
Next thing I know I'm in prison

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.090
and my call home

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:30.163
they say your little sister died.

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.740
Then, I don't know.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.600
I just wish I could
tell her how sorry I am

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.113
for the way I treated her.

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:45.300
I was a terrible big brother.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.860
I was not even a big brother to her.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.490
I always tried to push her away

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:50.790
and keep her away from me.

00:18:51.671 --> 00:18:53.400
I have no idea why,

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.360
maybe it was jealousy

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.890
because her father was in her life

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:57.970
and mine wasn't.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:59.360
Maybe that was the case,

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.193
I don't know.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.360
But I wish I could take it all back.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:05.740
My last thought of her

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:09.580
is her driving away in the car crying

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.830
because I wouldn't leave
with her to go home.

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:18.350
I felt all that guilt

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:20.070
when I got released,

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.943
and she passed away.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:24.840
All the guilt of treating her bad

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.010
hit me all at once

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.343
like a ton of bricks.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:33.210
And here I am after all these years

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.760
and she begged me to come home.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:36.783
I'm still here.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:39.473
And for what?

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.093
More worse stories?

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.130
At one point in time
when I was a teenager,

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.890
I was one of the best basketball players

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:02.903
in the county.

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:08.443
I was one of the best.

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:12.873
I mean, they were talking
like NBA type stuff,

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:14.920
but I didn't believe it.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:16.633
You know.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.950
Scouts would come in and look at us.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.113
I was in a boys home,

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:27.530
as it's, when I was a teenager.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.829
And people heard about
this team that we had,

00:20:30.829 --> 00:20:32.713
we was good, we was great.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.770
And I always ask myself,

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.853
what if I would've just
made the right decisions?

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.703
Could I be a retired NBA player by now?

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.393
Or whatever?

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:50.500
Could I have been anything

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.620
other than what I am today

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.200
if I would've made the right choice?

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.320
If I would've just listened to my dad.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.100
My dad's name is Raymond Johnson.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:58.980
Great man.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:20:59.883
He's a great man.

00:21:01.130 --> 00:21:02.163
He has a good heart.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.990
He's the only man that's
ever been there for me

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:09.823
the way he has

00:21:09.823 --> 00:21:11.113
and he's still there.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.350
Even though I'm doing what I'm doing,

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:18.773
he just wants me to do better,

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:22.063
as everybody else wants me to do.

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:25.670
I want the same thing too,

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:27.470
but what is it gonna take for me to,

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.640
give up, to say I'm tired?

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:34.160
What is it gonna take?

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.200
I don't wanna lose a limb

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:38.130
or even worse, lose my life.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.220
I don't want to be one of those

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:41.120
that dies down here

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:42.250
in some fucking tent

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:44.640
or on a sidewalk,

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:46.860
or while I'm sleeping,
a car jumps the curb

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:47.733
and ran me over.

00:21:49.628 --> 00:21:50.803
It happens.

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:54.900
People die while they sleep,

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:56.980
getting ran over by a car

00:21:56.980 --> 00:21:58.870
from an intoxicated driver

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:00.570
or something like that.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:03.690
How the fuck does a car jump the curb

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:04.693
if you're sober?

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:08.330
That wouldn't make sense.

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:09.233
Something's wrong.

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:16.423
If you have an addiction,

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:18.760
or there's something out there

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:20.630
that you really like doing.

00:22:20.630 --> 00:22:24.120
Whether it's alcohol, drugs, sex, food,

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:25.003
whatever it is,

00:22:28.310 --> 00:22:29.860
don't get carried away with it.

00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:33.133
Not even water.

00:22:33.133 --> 00:22:34.420
If you're addicted water,

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:35.623
it can be bad for you.

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:38.730
I had to, I learnt that.

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:39.940
Too much water is bad.

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:41.363
What the fuck is that?

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:45.695
Too much of anything could be harmful

00:22:45.695 --> 00:22:47.063
to the human body.

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:51.623
If you have a craving for something,

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:53.840
pray on it

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:54.673
and just

00:22:56.820 --> 00:22:57.653
don't do it,

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:01.030
because you're gonna feel bad

00:23:01.030 --> 00:23:03.040
once it's all over with.

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:06.710
Once you sold your belongings

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:10.830
and you're broke and no more drugs,

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:12.310
you're gonna feel bad

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:16.480
that you sold your shit to get high.

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:18.060
You're not even going to be high anymore

00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:19.860
so you're really gonna be assed out.

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:25.390
Drugs can make you do things

00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:28.187
that you never thought you would do.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:35.723
I went to prison for strong arm robbery.

00:23:39.468 --> 00:23:40.301
Um.

00:23:43.558 --> 00:23:46.475
And I robbed somebody buying drugs.

00:23:49.510 --> 00:23:50.780
I never thought I'd see,

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:52.913
see a day in prison in my life.

00:23:54.130 --> 00:23:54.963
As I was growing up,

00:23:54.963 --> 00:23:55.960
I might've been gangbanging

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:56.840
and doing whatever it is

00:23:56.840 --> 00:23:58.140
that I might've been doing,

00:23:58.140 --> 00:24:00.530
but I never saw myself going to prison,

00:24:00.530 --> 00:24:02.420
'cause even though I was
living that street life,

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:04.053
I still kept myself,

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:07.250
I don't know, it's something about school,

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:08.620
even though I don't like school.

00:24:08.620 --> 00:24:10.500
I do good in it when I put my,

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:11.333
when I,

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:13.380
when I go through with it.

00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:14.223
When I, when I,

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:17.023
push through the effort to,

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:22.023
to make an accomplishment.

00:24:23.930 --> 00:24:26.750
I haven't accomplished
many things in my life

00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:28.763
other than what you see now.

00:24:29.820 --> 00:24:32.340
The only accomplishment I've ever made was

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:35.347
making some beautiful kids.

00:24:35.347 --> 00:24:38.250
That's the only thing I have.

00:24:38.250 --> 00:24:39.623
So whenever I die,

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.100
there'll still be a part of me still here.

00:24:44.620 --> 00:24:47.863
A piece of me will still be here on Earth.

00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:52.960
Whether they, my kids know me, like me,

00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:53.793
or love me.

00:24:55.290 --> 00:24:58.280
And if they don't, I can understand,

00:24:58.280 --> 00:24:59.430
and I'm okay with that.

00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:02.513
I understand.

00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:05.683
You know.

00:25:07.520 --> 00:25:11.430
I'll still be here one way or the other

00:25:11.430 --> 00:25:13.453
to my daughters, to my sons,

00:25:14.690 --> 00:25:15.713
I'm still here.

00:25:22.050 --> 00:25:23.430
I wish.

00:25:23.430 --> 00:25:27.763
I wish that I never touched this stuff.

00:25:28.920 --> 00:25:29.753
Drugs, I mean.

00:25:32.900 --> 00:25:33.863
My mother,

00:25:35.050 --> 00:25:36.190
I started out smoking weed

00:25:36.190 --> 00:25:37.690
and she used to always say

00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:41.483
that weed is a gateway to other things.

00:25:42.360 --> 00:25:43.477
And I told her,

00:25:43.477 --> 00:25:45.760
"You don't know what you're talking about.

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:47.390
I'm not gonna do any other drugs."

00:25:47.390 --> 00:25:49.400
Even though I was
already doing other drugs

00:25:49.400 --> 00:25:50.473
when she said that.

00:25:53.330 --> 00:25:54.360
As much as I hate to say it,

00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:55.963
my mother was right.

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:02.970
She was right.

00:26:02.970 --> 00:26:04.570
She said, "Get you an education.

00:26:05.500 --> 00:26:06.670
When you get older

00:26:06.670 --> 00:26:08.560
you're gonna need it."

00:26:08.560 --> 00:26:09.473
She was right.

00:26:11.180 --> 00:26:13.430
I'm educated but I don't have it on paper.

00:26:13.430 --> 00:26:15.920
I don't have a high school diploma.

00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:19.610
Four different colleges,
I never got anything.

00:26:19.610 --> 00:26:20.610
I never graduated

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:24.470
because sooner or later
I choose to go back

00:26:24.470 --> 00:26:25.483
to the streets.

00:26:28.472 --> 00:26:29.670
I...

00:26:29.670 --> 00:26:31.690
I'm starting to get to the point where

00:26:31.690 --> 00:26:33.963
I am starting to feel a little, I'm tired,

00:26:35.490 --> 00:26:39.420
emotionally, mentally, physically,

00:26:39.420 --> 00:26:41.393
but mostly mentally.

00:26:43.090 --> 00:26:44.340
It's hard being out here,

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:49.603
especially when you let
people take advantage of you,

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:52.920
and use you,

00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:55.643
and they take your kindness for weakness,

00:26:55.643 --> 00:26:57.960
and your, and your,

00:26:57.960 --> 00:26:58.943
your humbleness.

00:26:59.850 --> 00:27:01.843
They take that shit for granted,

00:27:03.560 --> 00:27:04.393
not knowing

00:27:07.100 --> 00:27:08.973
who that person used to be,

00:27:09.820 --> 00:27:10.723
or could be.

00:27:11.810 --> 00:27:12.643
You never know.

00:27:14.360 --> 00:27:15.700
They'll never know about me,

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:16.653
what I was,

00:27:18.034 --> 00:27:19.884
because I refused to go back to that.

00:27:20.760 --> 00:27:22.160
I don't like hurting people.

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:28.240
I have to be,

00:27:28.240 --> 00:27:30.000
it takes a lot for me to get pissed off.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.563
It takes a hell of a lot.

00:27:33.330 --> 00:27:35.260
I mean, but after,

00:27:35.260 --> 00:27:37.683
at some point, everybody has,

00:27:38.920 --> 00:27:43.010
has a line that they draw.

00:27:43.010 --> 00:27:44.750
They can't take no more.

00:27:44.750 --> 00:27:45.583
So when I,

00:27:45.583 --> 00:27:47.590
when you finally respond
to some of the bullshit

00:27:47.590 --> 00:27:50.030
that people be throwing to you out here,

00:27:50.030 --> 00:27:51.370
they feel some type of way,

00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:53.210
because you're always the quiet one.

00:27:53.210 --> 00:27:56.780
You're always not responding to anything.

00:27:56.780 --> 00:27:58.193
Why the sudden change?

00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:03.070
Because it's gotta change somehow.

00:28:03.070 --> 00:28:05.793
At some point, no more disrespect.

00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.360
You gotta give respect in order to get it.

00:28:10.860 --> 00:28:12.560
Some people don't understand that.

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:14.943
They say common sense,

00:28:16.970 --> 00:28:17.803
everybody has it.

00:28:17.803 --> 00:28:19.610
And that's a lie.

00:28:19.610 --> 00:28:20.840
It should just be called sense

00:28:20.840 --> 00:28:22.260
'cause it's not very common,

00:28:22.260 --> 00:28:24.310
'cause everybody don't have common sense.

00:28:25.450 --> 00:28:26.680
Or maybe they do have it,

00:28:26.680 --> 00:28:28.630
they just haven't tapped into that yet.

00:28:33.910 --> 00:28:36.180
My eye is a result

00:28:37.570 --> 00:28:38.720
of me standing up

00:28:39.730 --> 00:28:41.323
for something that I believed.

00:28:46.640 --> 00:28:48.130
I'll say it again.

00:28:48.130 --> 00:28:51.146
You have to give respect
in order to get it.

00:28:51.146 --> 00:28:52.523
It is not just one way.

00:28:54.930 --> 00:28:56.243
This goes both ways.

00:28:57.310 --> 00:28:59.470
You can't expect to talk shit to somebody

00:28:59.470 --> 00:29:01.097
and expect for them to accept it

00:29:01.097 --> 00:29:02.090
and be cool with it

00:29:02.970 --> 00:29:04.900
without it eating them up inside.

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:06.680
That shit eats me up when I don't respond

00:29:06.680 --> 00:29:07.610
and kick somebody's ass

00:29:07.610 --> 00:29:08.490
or something like that.

00:29:08.490 --> 00:29:11.350
Or just go back and forth

00:29:11.350 --> 00:29:12.440
with the words with them.

00:29:12.440 --> 00:29:14.000
If I don't

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:16.640
and I just let it happen,

00:29:16.640 --> 00:29:18.450
it eats me up inside.

00:29:18.450 --> 00:29:19.767
It just builds up

00:29:19.767 --> 00:29:21.020
and I get mad at myself

00:29:21.020 --> 00:29:23.880
because I didn't do or say anything

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:24.793
to that person.

00:29:26.590 --> 00:29:28.490
But I do it anyway,

00:29:28.490 --> 00:29:30.283
because I know what I'm capable of.

00:29:32.010 --> 00:29:32.910
There's people out there

00:29:32.910 --> 00:29:34.810
that I don't want to see me like this.

00:29:36.070 --> 00:29:39.513
I want them to remember me for what I was.

00:29:40.830 --> 00:29:42.840
You know, the good things,

00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:43.673
I don't want them to see

00:29:43.673 --> 00:29:44.740
this new person.

00:29:44.740 --> 00:29:46.227
Like, "Who are you?"

00:29:48.380 --> 00:29:50.000
I want them to remember me

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:51.283
as I was back then.

00:29:53.630 --> 00:29:55.083
This person that they see now,

00:29:55.083 --> 00:29:57.440
that they could see now,

00:29:57.440 --> 00:29:59.090
they wouldn't know what to think.

00:30:00.490 --> 00:30:01.440
I had it all

00:30:02.510 --> 00:30:03.430
and I lost it all,

00:30:03.430 --> 00:30:04.393
just like that.

00:30:06.410 --> 00:30:08.473
All because of my bad decision-making.

00:30:10.710 --> 00:30:13.550
Everything that happens to me down here,

00:30:13.550 --> 00:30:14.850
I can't blame nobody but myself

00:30:14.850 --> 00:30:16.663
because I chose to be down here.

00:30:18.850 --> 00:30:19.800
The things that happened to me

00:30:19.800 --> 00:30:21.670
might not be my fault,

00:30:21.670 --> 00:30:23.090
but at the end of the day

00:30:23.090 --> 00:30:24.440
it's all my fault

00:30:24.440 --> 00:30:28.120
because I chose this over my family.

00:30:28.120 --> 00:30:30.573
I chose this over my health.

00:30:34.117 --> 00:30:35.457
"Let's get it together,"

00:30:36.650 --> 00:30:38.893
I keep telling myself that every day.

00:30:40.760 --> 00:30:42.690
And I feel the pressure of being tired

00:30:42.690 --> 00:30:43.560
of the streets.

00:30:43.560 --> 00:30:45.380
I'm starting to feel it now.

00:30:45.380 --> 00:30:47.913
Before, all these years, it wasn't,

00:30:49.030 --> 00:30:50.600
it wasn't on me like that,

00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:52.220
but for some reason I feel different

00:30:52.220 --> 00:30:53.570
about this shit now.

00:30:53.570 --> 00:30:55.220
The streets are boring.

00:30:55.220 --> 00:30:57.380
Everything's changed down here.

00:30:57.380 --> 00:30:58.830
It's not fun no more.

00:30:58.830 --> 00:30:59.763
It's bullshit.

00:31:01.031 --> 00:31:02.960
We have people snitching on each other.

00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:04.490
People hating on each other.

00:31:04.490 --> 00:31:05.323
And just,

00:31:07.620 --> 00:31:08.920
there's no love down here.

00:31:10.070 --> 00:31:11.870
It's all lies.

00:31:11.870 --> 00:31:13.663
Everything has a motive behind it.

00:31:15.080 --> 00:31:18.367
Can't believe nobody, can't trust 'em.

00:31:20.060 --> 00:31:21.180
So I don't get mad no more,

00:31:21.180 --> 00:31:22.013
I get even.

00:31:23.570 --> 00:31:24.660
I don't know why but

00:31:24.660 --> 00:31:27.650
I just had the craving

00:31:27.650 --> 00:31:29.680
to get even with people,

00:31:29.680 --> 00:31:32.203
or should I say, get even with Downtown.

00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:38.020
So, I stopped getting mad

00:31:38.020 --> 00:31:39.710
and just started doing things to people

00:31:39.710 --> 00:31:40.743
that they do to me.

00:31:42.630 --> 00:31:43.463
And they don't like it

00:31:43.463 --> 00:31:44.880
when I throw it back at them,

00:31:44.880 --> 00:31:45.830
they don't like it.

00:31:47.980 --> 00:31:49.130
I was that one person

00:31:49.130 --> 00:31:51.480
that would always say, "Yes."

00:31:51.480 --> 00:31:52.980
I don't like saying no to people.

00:31:52.980 --> 00:31:54.970
I just, I don't know why.

00:31:54.970 --> 00:31:55.990
I give people my last

00:31:55.990 --> 00:31:57.910
or whatever it is that they asked me for,

00:31:57.910 --> 00:31:58.833
if I can do it.

00:32:01.490 --> 00:32:03.120
I'm sick of that

00:32:03.120 --> 00:32:06.853
because at the end I'm
always the one that loses.

00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:09.033
And.

00:32:10.640 --> 00:32:13.513
I don't know, being
Downtown is very tiring.

00:32:14.770 --> 00:32:15.603
You know.

00:32:17.770 --> 00:32:19.230
It's draining.

00:32:19.230 --> 00:32:20.143
If you, if you,

00:32:22.210 --> 00:32:23.630
really think back on
all the shit that you,

00:32:23.630 --> 00:32:25.193
that I've been through,

00:32:26.190 --> 00:32:28.053
all the times I've been in jail.

00:32:28.950 --> 00:32:31.300
I can't count how many
times I've been in jail.

00:32:32.620 --> 00:32:34.330
I've been to jail more times than anybody

00:32:34.330 --> 00:32:35.813
that I can possibly think of,

00:32:38.020 --> 00:32:39.093
because of Downtown,

00:32:39.940 --> 00:32:43.620
and my continuous use of drugs.

00:32:43.620 --> 00:32:44.767
I had this...

00:32:49.114 --> 00:32:50.197
I don't know.

00:32:54.740 --> 00:32:56.190
It's time to get it together.

00:33:02.490 --> 00:33:03.450
I'm stuck, man.

00:33:03.450 --> 00:33:05.140
I don't know.

00:33:05.140 --> 00:33:06.930
It's hard.

00:33:06.930 --> 00:33:08.543
It gets real hard, man.

00:33:11.180 --> 00:33:12.360
It gets hard,

00:33:12.360 --> 00:33:15.043
but I can't be mad at nobody but myself,

00:33:16.610 --> 00:33:19.120
because I chose this over my kids,

00:33:19.120 --> 00:33:22.800
over my family, my grandparents,

00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:25.600
I chose this over everything.

00:33:25.600 --> 00:33:27.960
I have no connection
with nobody in my family.

00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:29.843
I don't know where nobody is.

00:33:34.740 --> 00:33:36.833
My dad is the only thing I got.

00:33:40.540 --> 00:33:42.143
I love my dad so much,

00:33:44.340 --> 00:33:45.890
because he never gave up on me.

00:33:48.010 --> 00:33:50.283
Even though I'm living this life,

00:33:51.480 --> 00:33:52.543
he's still there.

00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:55.300
No, I'm not asking him

00:33:55.300 --> 00:33:57.050
why he's giving me money all the time,

00:33:57.050 --> 00:33:59.740
but he will help me when he feel it

00:33:59.740 --> 00:34:00.683
that he needs to.

00:34:01.870 --> 00:34:04.470
But if he thinks I'm just on some bullshit

00:34:04.470 --> 00:34:07.333
and I'm asking him to
wire me money or whatever,

00:34:10.620 --> 00:34:12.220
for my addiction or whatever,

00:34:12.220 --> 00:34:13.990
he's not gonna help me.

00:34:13.990 --> 00:34:14.823
And I do understand,

00:34:14.823 --> 00:34:16.373
I understand completely,

00:34:18.300 --> 00:34:20.833
the disappointment is so great.

00:34:22.210 --> 00:34:25.270
I mean, I really had some
things going for myself

00:34:25.270 --> 00:34:26.220
when I was younger.

00:34:28.650 --> 00:34:29.960
Like I said before,

00:34:29.960 --> 00:34:31.530
all it takes is one

00:34:31.530 --> 00:34:33.593
and it could clean your whole life out.

00:34:34.440 --> 00:34:36.640
Take away everything just like that.

00:34:36.640 --> 00:34:38.240
I've seen people come down here,

00:34:39.340 --> 00:34:40.550
brand new cars,

00:34:40.550 --> 00:34:42.740
nice houses and shit.

00:34:42.740 --> 00:34:44.053
And they come down here.

00:34:44.999 --> 00:34:47.063
They started out as once or twice a week.

00:34:48.480 --> 00:34:51.100
Then it'll come to be every day

00:34:51.100 --> 00:34:52.420
they're coming down here.

00:34:52.420 --> 00:34:53.860
Now they're in the same car,

00:34:53.860 --> 00:34:56.310
but now it doesn't have that look anymore.

00:34:56.310 --> 00:34:58.520
And now it's just, I don't know,

00:34:58.520 --> 00:34:59.580
got a couple of dents

00:34:59.580 --> 00:35:01.480
or maybe a rim is missing

00:35:01.480 --> 00:35:03.523
and you're rolling on a donut wheel.

00:35:05.290 --> 00:35:07.773
I've seen people deteriorate.

00:35:08.770 --> 00:35:09.990
And what I mean by deteriorate,

00:35:09.990 --> 00:35:13.983
I've seen them lose things step by step.

00:35:15.070 --> 00:35:16.450
First is the house.

00:35:16.450 --> 00:35:17.530
They're not paying their rent no more,

00:35:17.530 --> 00:35:19.890
so they're sleeping in the car.

00:35:19.890 --> 00:35:20.990
Then they end up losing the car

00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:23.010
because they got too many tickets,

00:35:23.010 --> 00:35:24.200
'cause they're in the same parking space

00:35:24.200 --> 00:35:26.500
because they're sleeping in the car now.

00:35:26.500 --> 00:35:28.520
The car is full of all their clothes

00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:29.980
and belongings.

00:35:29.980 --> 00:35:30.813
And guess what?

00:35:30.813 --> 00:35:31.646
That's gonna get taken

00:35:31.646 --> 00:35:32.870
because somebody is
gonna break their window

00:35:32.870 --> 00:35:33.703
and take it all.

00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:38.010
Now, these same people are
out here pushing baskets

00:35:40.170 --> 00:35:41.683
and living on the street,

00:35:42.850 --> 00:35:45.070
due to the same shit that I did,

00:35:45.070 --> 00:35:46.703
because of bad decision-making.

00:35:48.850 --> 00:35:52.230
This drug or these drugs

00:35:52.230 --> 00:35:53.763
change your life forever.

00:35:56.590 --> 00:35:57.423
They really can.

00:36:02.170 --> 00:36:03.940
I've said this before

00:36:03.940 --> 00:36:05.930
but if I can go back
in time and change it,

00:36:05.930 --> 00:36:07.333
I would in a heartbeat.

00:36:11.290 --> 00:36:12.533
I'd give my right arm,

00:36:13.860 --> 00:36:17.700
any arm, I'd give whatever, a lung,

00:36:17.700 --> 00:36:18.830
just to go back in time

00:36:18.830 --> 00:36:21.233
and change my mistakes.

00:36:22.260 --> 00:36:24.530
I want to be there for my kids.

00:36:24.530 --> 00:36:26.910
I want to be a father.

00:36:26.910 --> 00:36:27.903
I want to be a dad.

00:36:29.870 --> 00:36:31.410
I'm a grandfather.

00:36:31.410 --> 00:36:35.540
And my grandkids, they're young.

00:36:35.540 --> 00:36:37.970
So, they're not old enough to understand

00:36:37.970 --> 00:36:40.420
what it is that I'm going through.

00:36:40.420 --> 00:36:42.913
But all my kids, they understand.

00:36:43.960 --> 00:36:45.203
My kids are smart.

00:36:47.900 --> 00:36:49.290
They're so smart

00:36:49.290 --> 00:36:51.263
and they still love their daddy.

00:36:52.900 --> 00:36:53.833
They love me.

00:36:58.130 --> 00:37:02.030
And I'm so ashamed of what I've become

00:37:02.030 --> 00:37:04.490
that I will not let them see me like this.

00:37:04.490 --> 00:37:05.710
I refuse

00:37:08.290 --> 00:37:10.633
to let my kids see me like this.

00:37:11.650 --> 00:37:13.110
My older ones,

00:37:13.110 --> 00:37:14.680
they see me a time or two

00:37:18.490 --> 00:37:19.463
in this condition.

00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:23.220
My daughter,

00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:24.453
my 21 year old,

00:37:26.100 --> 00:37:27.097
she came down here

00:37:27.097 --> 00:37:29.950
and I didn't even know she was coming.

00:37:29.950 --> 00:37:32.690
I hadn't seen her in
I don't know how long.

00:37:32.690 --> 00:37:35.193
And she turned around,

00:37:36.070 --> 00:37:37.737
she says, "Daddy."

00:37:39.230 --> 00:37:41.650
And I turned around.

00:37:41.650 --> 00:37:43.630
All I heard was that voice.

00:37:43.630 --> 00:37:46.100
And I turned around and
it's my little girl,

00:37:46.100 --> 00:37:47.173
my baby.

00:37:48.870 --> 00:37:50.770
That's the one that's gangbanging now.

00:37:53.590 --> 00:37:55.053
She loves her daddy so much.

00:38:01.022 --> 00:38:01.855
God, man.

00:38:03.480 --> 00:38:04.533
She loves her daddy.

00:38:12.380 --> 00:38:13.820
She grew up so hard.

00:38:13.820 --> 00:38:15.520
My daughter grew up

00:38:15.520 --> 00:38:17.123
without her parents.

00:38:18.620 --> 00:38:20.480
She didn't find out who her mother was

00:38:20.480 --> 00:38:21.873
until she was grown.

00:38:26.120 --> 00:38:27.780
She knew about me,

00:38:27.780 --> 00:38:29.550
but I was in and out

00:38:29.550 --> 00:38:32.320
because I wanted to live my life.

00:38:32.320 --> 00:38:33.920
I was selfish.

00:38:33.920 --> 00:38:36.000
I should have been there for her.

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:38.660
Maybe she wouldn't be where she is now.

00:38:38.660 --> 00:38:40.010
I mean, as far as the gangbanging

00:38:40.010 --> 00:38:42.610
and all the gang tats and stuff like that.

00:38:44.300 --> 00:38:46.310
My daughter, she's fully with the business

00:38:46.310 --> 00:38:47.520
in that hood shit.

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:48.553
She really is.

00:38:50.100 --> 00:38:51.440
But I want her to change her ways.

00:38:51.440 --> 00:38:53.770
My daughter has so much smarts

00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:55.220
she can do hair.

00:38:55.220 --> 00:38:56.250
She, she just,

00:38:56.250 --> 00:38:57.700
she graduated high school

00:38:57.700 --> 00:39:00.123
and I gave her thanks for that.

00:39:03.170 --> 00:39:04.003
I like to feel like

00:39:04.003 --> 00:39:05.630
I have something to do with that.

00:39:07.520 --> 00:39:09.700
Because if I wouldn't have been,

00:39:09.700 --> 00:39:10.533
if I would've been.

00:39:10.533 --> 00:39:11.623
Who's to say that,

00:39:12.690 --> 00:39:14.990
you know, I really do believe

00:39:14.990 --> 00:39:17.310
that things happen for a reason.

00:39:17.310 --> 00:39:18.910
Whether it's the smallest things

00:39:18.910 --> 00:39:20.380
to biggest things.

00:39:20.380 --> 00:39:22.850
Everything has a purpose.

00:39:22.850 --> 00:39:24.910
Every second, every minute, every hour,

00:39:24.910 --> 00:39:25.980
every movement,

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:27.870
everything that's going on around us

00:39:27.870 --> 00:39:29.940
has a purpose for some reason.

00:39:29.940 --> 00:39:32.210
And only God knows what it is.

00:39:32.210 --> 00:39:33.230
Who's to say that

00:39:33.230 --> 00:39:35.550
if I was there for my daughter,

00:39:35.550 --> 00:39:39.050
that just assuming she
wouldn't graduate high school,

00:39:39.050 --> 00:39:40.053
who knows?

00:39:41.760 --> 00:39:42.740
And this might sound silly

00:39:42.740 --> 00:39:47.300
but I feel like by me not
being there or whatever,

00:39:47.300 --> 00:39:48.600
whatever purpose might be,

00:39:53.210 --> 00:39:54.313
she graduated.

00:39:56.030 --> 00:39:56.960
As weird as it sounds

00:39:56.960 --> 00:39:58.810
I feel like I might,

00:39:58.810 --> 00:40:00.430
my bad decisions, whatever,

00:40:00.430 --> 00:40:02.250
however you want to call it.

00:40:02.250 --> 00:40:05.870
I had something to do
with that in some way.

00:40:05.870 --> 00:40:06.703
I don't know,

00:40:06.703 --> 00:40:08.043
but I feel that.

00:40:11.106 --> 00:40:15.273
But I won't even talk
about my daughter too much.

00:40:17.530 --> 00:40:20.100
I hope that one day if she sees this,

00:40:20.100 --> 00:40:22.173
baby, your daddy loves you very much.

00:40:23.280 --> 00:40:25.270
And I'm so proud of you,

00:40:25.270 --> 00:40:26.733
no matter what you decide to do

00:40:26.733 --> 00:40:27.653
with your life.

00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.280
You did something that
I was never able to do.

00:40:31.280 --> 00:40:32.233
You graduated.

00:40:33.140 --> 00:40:33.973
Good girl.

00:40:38.110 --> 00:40:39.090
I miss you.

00:40:39.090 --> 00:40:40.220
I love all my kids.

00:40:40.220 --> 00:40:41.880
I love all of you.

00:40:41.880 --> 00:40:42.713
Okay.

00:40:44.038 --> 00:40:44.871
Uh.

00:40:50.510 --> 00:40:51.547
Just say, "No."

00:40:54.170 --> 00:40:55.143
Go the other way.

00:40:59.530 --> 00:41:02.883
I know in life things happen.

00:41:06.290 --> 00:41:08.040
Just try to make the best decisions

00:41:08.040 --> 00:41:10.050
that you can for your future,

00:41:10.050 --> 00:41:11.960
for your kids' future,

00:41:11.960 --> 00:41:13.360
so you won't end up like me.

00:41:18.530 --> 00:41:19.363
I love you.

